    "reviews_wall": {
      "type": "tonelight-reviews",
      "blocks": {
        "review_1": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "stars": 5,
            "text": "Great stuff, very easy to handle, I can strongly recommend both the gear and the dealer/manufacturer. Many thanks!",
            "author": "Joachim B.",
            "product": "120 Easyloader tray (STL)",
            "date": "August 2026",
            "source": "tonephotographic.com"
          }
        },
        "review_2": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "stars": 5,
            "text": "I have scanned six 120 rolls with the Tone 120 dslr scanning system and it is a hit with me. )I also purchased the 35mm system, and have scanned two rolls so far. I paired them with an old laptop that I installed MX Linux 25.2 and Entangle to monitor the negatives as I turn the advancement dials. I like being able to sit down to scan. Finally, I can get perfectly aligned shots, and I can fill the frame using a geared Nikon GP-2 camera focusing stage to utilize the max resolution/area of the camera by raising and lowering the dslr in a controlled fashion. This also allows instant 90 degree orientation switching when going from 4.5x6 to 6x7 or half frame 35mm to full frame. Another wonderful feature is how easy it is to start the roll - just push it in until it contacts the silicone wheels, and start turning CCW. The Tone dslr scanning system is a well thought out and engineered system.",
            "author": "James M.",
            "product": "toneCarrier 120",
            "date": "July 2026",
            "source": "tonephotographic.com"
          }
        },
        "review_3": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "stars": 5,
            "text": "Great kit and easy to use with the printed parts! It gives the assembled tonecarrier some weight and sturdiness.",
            "author": "Jonas P.",
            "product": "toneCarrier hardware kit",
            "date": "July 2026",
            "source": "tonephotographic.com"
          }
        },
        "review_4": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "stars": 4,
            "text": "A well constructed piece of kit that has made my workflow more pleasurable and accessible. Solid and smooth to operate. Only issue has been film catching occasionally on the self spooling module.",
            "author": "Malcolm S.",
            "product": "toneCarrier 120 kit",
            "date": "July 2026",
            "source": "tonephotographic.com"
          }
        },
        "review_5": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "stars": 5,
            "text": "Best Scanning kit i used so far. Film always lays perfectly flat and super easy to advance. Bought the 35mm version assembled and 3D printed the 120 one. Both work flawlessly. Thanks!",
            "author": "Stefano V.",
            "product": "toneCarrier 35 mm kit",
            "date": "June 2026",
            "source": "tonephotographic.com"
          }
        },
        "review_6": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "stars": 5,
            "text": "I got tired of the vignetting and squeaking mechanism of my Valoi360 system and got frustrated when I ordered their scanning hood and received an overpriced, cheaply 3D-printed plastic tube. Of course, I have nothing against 3D-printed items. I own a 3D printer myself, so I know when they are cheaply printed versus printed well, with thin layers and thick walls. So I decided to look for an alternative film carrier I could print myself, found the basic 35mm ToneCarrier on MakerWorld, and was impressed by the quality and attention to detail of the model, which brought me to this site. I purchased both the 35mm and 120 carrier 3D models, and I'm extremely impressed with their quality, how well documented everything is, and how easy they are to print and assemble. I'm more than happy I made the move from Valoi to ToneCarrier.",
            "author": "Richard P.",
            "product": "toneCarrier 35 mm (STL)",
            "date": "June 2026",
            "source": "tonephotographic.com"
          }
        },
        "photos_1": {
          "type": "photos",
